# Nemotron Nano 9B v2 Q4_K_L, with layer placement forced rather than inferred.
#
# Why this exists: Ollama's automatic placement left 15% of this model's layers
# on CPU and delivered 12.7 tok/s, where llama.cpp with `-ngl 99` on the same
# file, same quant, same host reached 42.65 tok/s -- a 3.4x difference that was
# entirely placement, not hardware (M0 findings entry 1, addendum 3, 2026-09-15).
#
# The llama.cpp route was then abandoned for a different reason: llama-server
# runs under WSL, whose `.wslconfig` cap is 4.3 GiB against a 6.7 GB model, and
# it was killed mid-sweep twice. Ollama runs natively on Windows and has no such
# cap, so forcing placement here removes the WSL dependency entirely -- if the
# residency actually lands.
#
# num_gpu 99 = offload every layer. Ollama clamps to what fits, so this is a
# request, not a guarantee: check `ollama ps` for size_vram against size and do
# not assume it worked.
FROM nemotron-nano-9b-v2-q4kl:latest

PARAMETER num_gpu 99
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192
